🟡 **Medium** `Adapters/ClaudeAdapterV2.ts:4113`

When the session version is below the error’s required version, `claudeRewrittenVersion` still returns the gateway’s older reported version, causing the caller to replace the error and discard the CLI upgrade requirement. The regex captures only the reported version; capture the required version too and only rewrite when the session meets it, otherwise retain the original error.

```diff
-  /^API Error: 400 Claude Code (\d+\.\d+\.\d+) does not support this model; version \d+\.\d+\.\d+ or newer is required\./;
+  /^API Error: 400 Claude Code (\d+\.\d+\.\d+) does not support this model; version (\d+\.\d+\.\d+) or newer is required\./;
+
+  const match = CLAUDE_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION_ERROR.exec(message.result.trim());
+  const reported = match?.[1];
+  const required = match?.[2];
+  return reported !== undefined &&
+    required !== undefined &&
+    sessionVersion !== undefined &&
+    compareSemverVersions(sessionVersion, required) >= 0 &&
+    compareSemverVersions(reported, sessionVersion) < 0
+    ? reported
+    : undefined;

```

